<!--
    SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright (c) Rikarin
    SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

    Doc 36 § F7 wave 7. The foliage palette: what is in it, and which of its entries a stroke would
    place. One of the two parts the Foliage panel is made of, ported for the reason `FactBlock`'s
    header gives — the panel builds directly into a `DockPanel`, so it is its parts that become
    markup and not the panel.

    ⚠ **Two shapes of row, and the empty state is the interesting one.** An empty palette shows *why*
    it is empty, which is a plain `FactRow` — "add a .vxfoliage or .vxgrass to the palette", or
    whatever the mode is refusing over. Entering a mode that does nothing and says nothing is the
    state every one of these toolsets puts a new user in, and that sentence is the cure. A palette
    with entries in it is a `fact-row` per type with a check box in it.

    ⚠ **The two arms are chosen by an `@if` around the whole loop, not inside it.** The empty state
    is not a row of the list — it is a different list — so the `@if` is `Switch` at the top level of
    the part and each arm builds its own thing. Nothing here closes over a pattern variable, which is
    wave 4's rule: the arm's condition is `Empty`, and everything either arm reads goes back through
    the signal.

    ⚠ **`change:IsChecked` and no `refs`, because a row's handler needs nothing but its own slot.**
    `refs` earns its keep when a handler has to reach a *sibling* control — the mixer's fader reading
    its own mute — or when a plain element has to be hit-tested. Here the handler closes over
    `entry.Slot`, which is in the key, so the row it belongs to is the row it was built for.

    ⚠ **The write-back cannot loop.** Ticking a box calls `Chosen`, which the panel answers by
    calling `Show` again — and the `IsChecked` binding that assignment re-runs is the one whose
    `change:` handler started it. It terminates because a change made while effects are draining is
    not reported, which is the rule `TextureImportView`'s channel bar rests on too.

    ⚠ **`@inherits Vixen.Ui.UiElement` and not `Control`**, for `FactBlock`'s reason: a `Control`
    gives itself `variant-default` and `size-md`, and `panel.Add("foliage-palette")` had neither.
-->
@component PaletteBlock
@namespace Vixen.Editor.Terrain
@inherits Vixen.Ui.UiElement
@tag foliage-palette
@using System.Collections.Immutable
@using Vixen.Editor.Ui
@using Vixen.Ui
@using Vixen.Ui.Controls
@using Vixen.Ui.Reactive

@if (Empty) {
    <FactRow Name="No types" Value="@Refusal" />
} else {
    @for (var entry in Rows) {
        <fact-row key="@entry">
            <CheckBox Label="@entry.Name"
                      IsChecked="@entry.Chosen"
                      change:IsChecked="@(on => Choose(entry.Slot, on))" />

            <fact-value>@entry.Detail</fact-value>
        </fact-row>
    }
}

@code {
    /// <inheritdoc cref="Show" />
    readonly Signal<ImmutableArray<PaletteEntry>> rows = new([]);

    /// <inheritdoc cref="Empty" />
    readonly Signal<string> refusal = new(string.Empty);

    /// <summary>What is in the palette, in the order the volume declares it.</summary>
    public IReadOnlyList<PaletteEntry> Entries => rows.Value;

    /// <summary>Runs when an entry is added to or taken out of what a stroke would place.</summary>
    /// <remarks>
    ///     The slot and the new state, because the panel's own <c>Choose</c> takes exactly those two
    ///     — additive selection is the mode's business and not this part's.
    /// </remarks>
    public Action<int, bool>? Chose { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Shows a palette.</summary>
    /// <param name="entries">What is in it, in order.</param>
    /// <exception cref="ArgumentNullException"><paramref name="entries" /> is null.</exception>
    public void Show(IEnumerable<PaletteEntry> entries) {
        ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(entries);

        rows.Value = [.. entries];
        refusal.Value = string.Empty;
    }

    /// <summary>Shows an empty palette, and why it is empty.</summary>
    /// <param name="why">What the mode is refusing over, or the sentence telling an author what to add.</param>
    /// <exception cref="ArgumentException"><paramref name="why" /> is empty.</exception>
    public void ShowNothing(string why) {
        ArgumentException.ThrowIfNullOrEmpty(why);

        rows.Value = [];
        refusal.Value = why;
    }

    void Choose(int slot, bool on) => Chose?.Invoke(slot, on);

    // ================================================================== What the markup reads

    bool Empty => rows.Value.Length == 0;

    string Refusal => refusal.Value;

    ImmutableArray<PaletteEntry> Rows => rows.Value;
}
